// A knowledge-propagation web for an incident response team — the structural
// half of the language, in one coherent scenario. Who was told what, who is
// accountable, who may access the incident, and who holds the root cause.
//
// This example is about *structure*, so it exercises the set/relation/quantifier
// machinery: SET, CLOSE, TOTAL, FOR EACH ... IN, FOR EACH ... MENTIONED,
// EXISTS/WITNESS, ONEOF, ATLEAST, FORBIDS, UNLESS, PREFERS, ASSUME, VAR.
//
// Expected result: CONSISTENT — every constraint holds; the derivations below
// show the closures, the quantified rules firing, and a preference resolving a
// clash. Free atoms (who else was paged, etc.) stay UNKNOWN, as they should.

DOMAIN team

SET agents
    ana
    ben
    cal

// --- Knowledge flows along "told", declared transitive with CLOSE: ana told ben
//     and ben told cal complete to ana told cal (a DAG — CLOSE … TRANSITIVE
//     forbids cycles). Each written edge briefs the next agent into the loop. ---
FACT ana told ben
FACT ben told cal
CLOSE told TRANSITIVE

RULE direct_reach:
    WHEN ana told ben
    THEN ben in_loop
RULE relay_reach:
    WHEN ben told cal
    THEN cal in_loop

// --- Every agent must have a briefing source. `briefed_by` pairs are the witness
//     table; TOTAL checks each element of `agents` appears as a subject. ---
FACT ana briefed_by ana          // ana is the origin — her own source
FACT ben briefed_by ana
FACT cal briefed_by ben
TOTAL briefed_by ON agents

// --- A universal over the declared set: every briefed agent is accountable. ---
RULE accountable FOR EACH x IN agents:
    WHEN x is_briefed
    THEN x accountable

// --- A universal over everyone MENTIONED anywhere (open — no SET needed): an
//     on-call agent gets clearance. ---
RULE has_clearance FOR EACH y MENTIONED:
    WHEN y on_call
    THEN y has_clearance

FACT ana is_briefed
FACT ana on_call

// --- Exactly one incident commander. ---
PREMISE one_commander:
    ONEOF
        ana is_commander
        ben is_commander
        cal is_commander
FACT ana is_commander

// --- At least one responder is paged. ---
PREMISE someone_paged:
    ATLEAST
        ana paged
        ben paged
        cal paged
FACT ben paged

// --- An existential over an OPEN population: some agent holds the root cause.
//     The author names the WITNESS; the engine checks it actually holds. ---
FACT ana holds_root_cause
PREMISE cause_is_held:
    EXISTS h WITNESS ana
        h holds_root_cause

// --- Two default clearance rules clash for an on-call agent. PREFERS declares
//     which wins: on-call access is restricted, overriding the broad default. ---
RULE broad_access:
    WHEN ana on_call
    THEN ana full_access
RULE oncall_is_restricted:
    WHEN ana on_call
    THEN NOT ana full_access
PREFERS oncall_is_restricted OVER broad_access

// --- Trusted by default, UNLESS explicitly flagged (a defeasible rule). ben is
//     flagged, so his default trust is retracted; ana keeps hers. ---
RULE trusted_by_default FOR EACH z IN agents:
    WHEN z accountable
    THEN z trusted
    UNLESS z flagged
FACT ben accountable
FACT ben flagged

// --- A guard: the commander must not be a flagged agent. ---
PREMISE clean_commander:
    FORBIDS
        ana is_commander
        ana flagged

// --- A retractable working hypothesis, put to work by a rule so it is not idle. ---
ASSUME cal available
RULE standby:
    WHEN cal available
    THEN cal can_respond

// --- A toggle port with a default (shows up as a PARAM in the report). ---
VAR maintenance_mode DEFAULT false

// --- Plain abduction (no goal): is "cal available" consistent with everything? ---
TRY cal available

CHECK
